# Budget/parser/index implementation handoff

This child owns only semantic_profile_restore_budget.py in its independent tree/branch from ddcf5ed. The parent owns integration, complete runtime tests and final review. No inherited 68 input, other three new writers, protected AGENTS, Goal, paid/model/GUI/native/e2e/HMR/push/PR/merge action was changed or executed here.

## Frozen interfaces

- RestoreLedger(overrides=()) uses exact tuple pairs, lower-only at begin(B,Q,N). B/Q/N/J/S are read-only properties. Fixed caps and work usage/live/peaks/slot_states are immutable tuples. begin is single-use; finish(False) accepts an entry failure before begin and preserves an already-terminal state by rejecting reuse. finish does not manufacture successful slots.
- charge(work_domain,amount,stage=...), reserve(live_domain,amount,stage=...), release(live_domain,amount), visit, prepay(stage), opaque(), start_slot/complete_slot, cleanup, finish. Cleanup/release do not spend an exhausted work pool. cleanup is called only after the parent actually drops temporaries or transfers result ownership; it is accounting cleanup, not a garbage-collection claim.
- Work domains: wire, schema, traversal, integer, copy, cache_query, cache_split, cache_alloc, rule, pv_compare, hash. Live domains: scalar, objects, trie_nodes, trie_slots, opaque_scalar, opaque_objects. Caps exactly use approved section 6; no new scalar work cap or reuse of T05 pools.
- read_json(raw,ledger,label='payload') returns ordinary safe AST only. Labels payload/rows/input/source. It owns raw accounting already reserved by begin; it additionally owns AST node/slot and decoded string reservations until parent cleanup. The UTF8 whole-text and lexical fixed-stack reservations are released locally. Root native construction must not count reused strings as copied new values.
- hex_integer(text,ledger,stage='A2') and hex_bytes(text,ledger,maximum=...,stage='A2') return their native scalar with retained logical tickets; parent cleanup owns them. No native JSON number path.
- term_key(exact TermInput,ledger) uses 8-byte header, source flag, fixed eight marker/4-byte lengths, complete UTF8. Source None and all-None SourceRecord differ. Returned bytes owns scalar=len(key), objects=1; always release_key after cache lookup. It does not normalize RDF, language or datatype.
- TermCache(ledger).get_or_insert(key,factory) returns value; factory is a private trusted closure, not entry data. It prepays key + 65536 scalar/16 object strong-value holdings before factory, so the parent must not double-reserve them. Each cache clear drops actual references and releases its own holdings; caller's returned native objects may continue owning the same issued value after handoff. No old alias/issuer identity is asserted.
- canonical_bytes(safe_projection,ledger,stage=...,bound=...) is for already-validated safe internal projection, not an arbitrary object JSON API. It prepays the stage once, reserves buffers capped by min(bound,B+Q), and delegates the unchanged fixed _profile_json_bytes under opaque peak. Caller must not nest another opaque context. Returned bytes owns len(result) scalar/one object; consume then release_bytes.
- digest(raw,ledger,stage=...) precharges SHA input length and retains the 64-character/one-object output until cleanup. Cache audit directly precharges separator+key and invokes module sha256/update/hexdigest without concatenating a long key. Its output is never used for cache equality; a test can monkeypatch module sha256 to a constant hasher while canonical rule_profile fingerprint remains real.

## Operations and allocation mapping

A1 UTF8 prepay, lexical scan and build are separate three wire reads. The preflight checks depth35, cumulative value/key nodes <=B+Q, duplicate fixed keys, all string escapes/surrogates and length bounds before value-string/container construction. The second scan constructs only after those gates. Keys are selected by full comparison from fixed literal JSON_KEYS before dict insertion; each object has at most32 keys and each key at most64 UTF8 bytes. No attacker key hash table is used for discovery. Main positional schemas still reject a globally valid key/tag in the wrong place.

Before string construction the lexical pass applies source-field65KiB, term-field16KiB, inthex8195B, byteshex524288B, rows8192characters, recordType64B and the remaining original projection-character limit. No original comparison/head/source field is omitted. Integer conversion prepays the approved q(q+1)+8h+16 block before chunked at-most8-hex-digit shifts/OR and reserves maximum temporary limb/hex storage. byteshex checks lowercase/even/child maximum before bytes.fromhex and retains decoded bytes tickets.

A4 full-key sizing scans each complete field after paying its character count; output size and complete UTF8/framing writes are prepaid. Key temporary buffer/bytes and fixed framing metadata are reserved before allocation. Every cache lookup records full occurrence/key bytes against M/S and pays key SHA even on hit. Each edge is only a (complete-key reference,start,end) view. Sparse child vectors contain <=256 native entries, with one precharged native-byte comparison per scanned child. Prefix comparison prepays min(remaining,edge length), even if the first byte mismatches, and advances key position monotonically. Splits never slice/copy a long key tail.

Each node prepays320 fixed allocation/update units and reserves one trie-node/256-branch-slot tickets; each miss64 and each lookup16 extra update units. Sparse-vector append prepays a full old-vector copy even if Python reuses capacity; <=256U such copy units fit the approved512U domain. A linked allocation chain avoids an unbounded flat-node-vector copy. Cleanup touches <=2U+N nodes and <=2U populated branch refs, covered by the node64-metadata/miss64 prepayment, requiring no new debit after a resource failure. It clears node key/value/children/next references without recursive trie traversal.

Canonical projection/encoding stages prepay32J traversal plus4(B+Q+S) copy; fixed-key encoder sorting also reserves128J in the existing schema domain. Only existing delegation stages should call prepay; own A1-A6 loops charge actual units. This does not promise arbitrary additional passes fit the approved schedule. The existing canonical parse and 16c work/encoding/hash remain within their own original budgets; opaque reserves their source-derived logical peak before a call, not after measuring usage and not by a fake internal hook.

## Actually run

Standalone harness is under this child evidence directory. The first command used system python3 (3.9), which could not import the inherited slots=True dataclass; its full failure is retained. No dependency or environment was copied/installed to repair it. The second and final commands used the existing read-only CPython3.12 runtime with this child's PYTHONPATH and passed.

The harness checked six valid JSONs, eighteen invalid/boundary JSONs, canonical/invalid/32768-bit integer forms, byte-hex rejection, five complete-key source/language distinctions, all256 branch bytes, 82 keys with30000-byte shared prefixes including shorter-prefix split, artificial identical audit SHA with distinct full-key values, lower wire/opaque failure before the operation, and terminal ledger reuse rejection. It is not full production->JSON->exec restoration, not all integration tests, not performance/RSS/GC evidence, and does not replace parent independent review. Final check output contains actual logical usage/peaks. The parent will run the required final formatter/lint/check/sources in its own isolated environment after per-path integration.
